  <static seed="99" source="Contrib/DMOI/1-Counting/1_2-Binomial_Coefficients/1_2_7.pg">
    <statement><p>How many subsets of <m>\{0,1,\ldots, 9\}</m> have cardinality 8 or more?</p>
<p><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <hint><p>Break the question into 3 cases.</p>
</hint>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>56</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>This is the same as a question about 8-bit strings, since we can think of each subset as a 8-bit string with a 1 representing that we include that element in the subset.  <m>{10 \choose 8} + {10\choose 9} + \cdots + {10\choose 10} = {56}</m> subsets.</p>
</solution>
